# WBUX6-W4-A-01. Generated ux-map markdown: `docs/ux-maps/render_ux_maps.py` is the only
# writer. Prettier reflows the render, the next render undoes the reflow, and the two
# rewrite each other forever — a derived artifact gets exactly one owner (DATA-14).
# Note the deliberate asymmetry: the sibling `*.uxmap.json` files are HAND-AUTHORED
# sources and Prettier IS their owner, so they must stay formatted. Do not "consistently"
# add them here.
docs/ux-maps/*.md

# WBUX6-W4-A-07. `render_ux_maps.py` lives beside the maps it renders, and Prettier has
# no Python parser: any aggregate glob over `docs/ux-maps/**` that is not extension-scoped
# dies with `No parser could be inferred` instead of checking the maps. Ignoring the
# generator keeps a directory-wide glob a safe thing to write.
docs/ux-maps/*.py
# ...and the bytecode CPython drops beside it the first time anyone runs the
# generator. `*.py` does not cover `__pycache__/*.pyc`, so the glob still died.
docs/ux-maps/**/__pycache__/
